          <h4 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-space-blue-light mb-4">
            Magnetar Outbursts & The FRB Connection
          </h4>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed">
            Magnetars are currently the leading progenitor candidates for Fast Radio Bursts (FRBs). However, the exact trigger mechanisms and energy partition during an outburst remain unsolved. My research focuses on the multi-wavelength evolution of these extreme events. I have led deep X-ray and radio campaigns during the reactivations of 
            <a href="https://doi.org/10.3847/1538-4357/ad293b" 
               target="_blank" 
               rel="noopener noreferrer" 
               class="underline font-medium hover:text-space-blue-light">
              SGR J1935+2154 <span class="text-xs align-super">[Ibrahim et al. 2024]</span>
            </a>
            and 
            <a href="https://doi.org/10.3847/1538-4357/aca528" 
               target="_blank" 
               rel="noopener noreferrer" 
               class="underline font-medium hover:text-space-blue-light">
              Swift J1818.0–1607 <span class="text-xs align-super">[Ibrahim et al. 2023]</span>
            </a>,
            integrating data from XMM-Newton, NuSTAR, and the VLA to characterize their broadband spectral and timing evolution.
          </p>
        </div>
